+Customize the metrics response
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+You can define a ``__metrics__`` method on your Service class to modify the raw Prometheus metrics text returned by the ``/metrics`` endpoint. The method receives the metrics text as a string and must return the modified string, which is then served as the response. It can be synchronous or asynchronous.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    import bentoml
+
+    @bentoml.service
+    class MyService:
+        def __metrics__(self, metrics_content: str) -> str:
+            # Append a custom metric line to the default metrics output
+            return metrics_content + '\nmy_custom_metric 1.0\n'
+
+The ``/metrics`` endpoint is only registered when metrics are enabled (``metrics.enabled``, which is ``True`` by default).
+
 An example with custom metrics
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
